---
/**
 * t50 · Caustic
 *
 * The body treated as a lens. A curved transparent wall does not merely pass
 * light, it *steers* it, and light steered by a curve does not land evenly:
 * it bunches into a bright, narrow seam a short way inside the far wall. That
 * seam is a caustic — the bright wobbling line at the bottom of a swimming
 * pool, the crescent inside a wine glass on a table.
 *
 * So the far shoulder here is drawn as three things stacked in order from the
 * edge inward: a dark outer ring where the beam leaves the glass, then the
 * caustic seam riding one to three rings in, then the calm field. The near
 * wall gets only a modest entry glow, because a lens spends its light on the
 * far side, not the near one. Deliberately the dimmest of the four overall,
 * so the seam has somewhere to be bright *against*.
 *
 * One silhouette, four lights. t47-t50 share a single conventional bubble —
 * a 28x22 rounded body on rows 2-23 and a five-row tail dropped from its
 * bottom-left corner, its left edge flush with the body wall and its
 * hypotenuse a clean 45-degree staircase to a blunt two-pixel tip. Nothing
 * about the shape changes between the four. Only the optics do, so any
 * difference you can see is a difference in how the material behaves.
 *
 * The tail is not an appliqué. It is part of the same solid, so it is sampled
 * from the same normal field and the same ring depth as the body and takes
 * whatever the variant's light is doing at that corner. The ink outline
 * traces the union of body and tail exactly, one pixel wide, with no seam
 * where they meet.
 *
 * The face is `md` with the `compact` smile at gap 2 — eight rows by eight
 * columns — centred on the bubble **body**, tail ignored: 7 rows of air above
 * and 7 below, measured. Nothing is cleared behind it; every tone it lands on
 * clears 4.5:1 against white.
 *
 * 8 tones.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Caustic">
